# Support Vector Machines (SVM): Generalization, Kernel Methods, and Noise Robustness

**Course:** Machine Learning and Neural Networks for Neuroscience (`27504-01`) — Bar-Ilan University  
**Assignment:** Homework 2 — Support Vector Machines (SVM)

---

## Overview

This repository contains the Python implementation, visualization scripts, and empirical analysis for 
**Homework 2**, which investigates how linear and kernel-based Support Vector Machines behave under varying
geometric structures, Gaussian data augmentations, training label corruption, and high-dimensional feature spaces.

All experiments use a fixed random seed (`seed=42`) to ensure full reproducibility across runs.

